THOUGHT: The syntax error is due to a missing closing brace after the second insert call; I need to restore the original if-block structure and then add a clean null check after the block. I’ll fix lines 690–697 to properly close the if (node == null) block and then add `if (node == null) return null;` before using node, and then re-run the Gradle compile to ensure there are no PixmapPacker errors and that the NullAway error count decreased by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '690,697c\      if (node == null) {
        // Didn'''t fit, pack into a new page.
        page = new GuillotinePage(packer);
        packer.pages.add(page);
        node = insert(page.root, rect);
      }
      if (node == null) return null;
      node.full = true;
      rect.set(node.rect.x, node.rect.y, node.rect.width - padding, node.rect.height - padding);
      return page;' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/PixmapPacker.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && { echo "---- PixmapPacker-related errors ----"; grep -n "PixmapPacker" new_build_output.log || true; echo "---- NullAway error summary ----"; grep -n "NullAway" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 || true; }
```

